<section class="band">
  <h2 class="section-title">Bravo with a Go</h2>
  <p class="section-intro">Paired with a Go, Bravo passes ADS-B traffic to it. The Go shows ADS-B, ADS-L and FLARM on one radar. The Go keeps broadcasting your position in ADS-L. Together they make a skyBlip Tango.</p>
  <p class="more"><%= link_to_page "skyblip-tango", label: "What a Tango does" %></p>
</section>

<section class="band band--tint">
  <h2 class="section-title">Your questions, answered</h2>
  <div class="faq">
    <details>
      <summary>Does Bravo make me visible?</summary>
      <p>No. Bravo does not transmit your position. To be seen in ADS-L, you need a Go, alone or paired with your Bravo as a Tango.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Does the X1 receive ADS-B with Meshtastic?</summary>
      <p>No. Meshtastic does not receive ADS-B. Bravo needs the skyBlip firmware. Install it by USB-C using the steps above.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>My aircraft has a transponder. Does its own signal show as traffic?</summary>
      <p>No, once you enter your aircraft&rsquo;s ICAO address on Bravo or on the Go paired with it. Bravo then leaves your own transponder out of the traffic it sends.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Why does Bravo need no activation or account?</summary>
      <p>Only a device that transmits in ADS-L needs its own address from skyBlip&rsquo;s range in the ADS-L registry. The Go gets it at activation, while Bravo transmits nothing and needs neither activation nor an account.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Do I need a Go?</summary>
      <p>No. Bravo sends ADS-B traffic directly to your navigation app over Bluetooth. Its buzzer and vibration motor warn you of approaching traffic. A Go is an optional next step if you want to receive ADS-L and FLARM traffic and broadcast your position in ADS-L. Paired with Bravo, it forms a <%= link_to_page "skyblip-tango", label: "Tango" %> and shows all three kinds of traffic on its radar.</p>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Do I need a ground station?</summary>
      <p>No. Bravo receives ADS-B in the aircraft, wherever the signal reaches it.</p>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>
